silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_02_preservation_laws_as_transport_correctness_sections_04_preservation_failures_as_transport_pathologies_concrete_anchor silm:hasExample "In 'PreservationFailuresAsTransportPathologiesConcreteAnchor', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, F1 pathology: the transport sends a household identity to a non-identity self-loop on the clinic side; also, F1 pathology: the transport simply drops the household identity arrow; the clinic patient image has no identity declared; also, F2 pathology: the transport sends the household composite to a clinic arrow not equal to the composite of the transports." .
